# Overlay applied on top of aports' community/firefox/mozconfig.
#
# aports' mozconfig is already tuned for an Alpine distro build (system libs,
# release channel, hardening on, updater off). What it is NOT tuned for is
# speed: aports puts every optimisation in the APKBUILD's build() function,
# which we never run because we invoke ./mach build directly. `base-mozconfig`
# has zero mentions of `lto` and carries `--disable-jemalloc`, so what we
# shipped was the distro's SOURCE with none of the distro's optimisation.
#
# `apply-and-build.sh` builds .mozconfig as `cat aports/mozconfig overlay`, so
# options here are appended and win over the base.
#
# We do enable sccache here so mach wraps every CC / rustc invocation, which
# combined with the Dockerfile cache mount makes incremental rebuilds across
# CI runs fast (3h cold → ~5min hot).
ac_add_options --with-ccache=sccache

# PERF ARM (perf/firefox-lto-jemalloc). Measured against PW's own firefox on a
# single runner, our build's only real deltas are screenshot 1.20, launch 1.16
# and layout 1.09, while every JIT-executed kernel is at parity — the shape a
# missing C++ optimisation makes. Two of the three missing levers, in one
# build; PGO is the third and costs roughly twice this.
#
# jemalloc: base sets --disable-jemalloc, and the shipped libxul.so has zero
# moz_arena_ symbols, so firefox runs on musl malloc. An LD_PRELOAD A/B in the
# shipped image (mimalloc vs musl malloc, one container, back to back) moved
# eval_rtt -33%, launch -21%, layout -12% while the allocation-free controls
# stayed flat (libm_fmod +1%, locator_click -2%) — so the allocator is real,
# but it only bought 5% of screenshot.
ac_add_options --enable-jemalloc

# lto: aports uses exactly `cross` in its optimised-mozconfig. Kept identical
# rather than dropping to `cross,thin`, because `cross` is the recipe proven to
# build firefox on Alpine x86_64. If the final link OOMs on a 4-vCPU/16GB
# runner, `--enable-lto=cross,thin` is the fallback — and the failure would
# land late, at the link step.
ac_add_options --enable-lto=cross
